Title: Make the R15 residue inventory cover every lifecycle surface and filesystem escape
Created: 2026-09-04
Author: codex

--- log ---
2026-09-04T10:00Z codex created

--- body ---

## Context

Child of tracker `0648`. `R15-residue-inventory` watches regular files created
inside its arena during `install`. It can pass when state is created outside the
arena, when an empty directory or other owned filesystem entry survives, or
when an offered later lifecycle surface creates the undeclared state.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] define the complete set of lifecycle surfaces the inventory must exercise
- [ ] prevent or observe writes outside the arena so an invisible escape cannot
      produce `pass`
- [ ] account for owned directories, symlinks and other applicable filesystem
      entries, not regular files alone
- [ ] preserve explicit, narrow handling of user data and external configuration
- [ ] red controls independently cover an outside-arena escape, a non-file
      residue, and state created after install
- [ ] `make check` passes
